{# "Latest files kept" — this module's cell on the HOST's organization
   dashboard (`/`). Design: org.widgets.js, the `files` cell, composed by
   preset E.

   Rendered by the host with `with_context: false`, so everything readable
   here arrives in one map: this module's own reading under `by.storage`,
   plus the shared `scope` and `now` the host composes. Nothing in this file
   may reach for a global.

   THE VOCABULARY IS THE HOST'S. `.c`, `.tab`, `.src`, `.more`, `.tbl` and
   `.ao-by` belong to the surface these cells sit on — the area bundle ships
   them and this module defines none of them.

   NO WIDGET INDEX. The design prints FI·G2 in the tab; that is the
   workspace's referencing system and not product
   (tests/Unit/Template/NoWorkshopLabelsTest).

   BOUNDED. A dashboard cell's height may not grow with its data, so the
   table stops at `by.storage.rows` and the tab states the total rather than
   hiding it. #}
{% set fi = by.storage %}
<div class="c" data-w="files">
    <span class="tab">Latest files kept<span class="src">&middot; {{ fi.thisWeek }} this week &middot; {{ fi.bytes|storage_bytes }} in all</span></span>
    {# WHOSE FIGURE THIS IS. The day this module is uninstalled the cell goes
       with it, and the tag is what makes that read as the system working
       rather than as something missing. #}
    <span class="ao-by"><i></i>files</span>
    {% if fi.registerUrl %}<a class="more" href="{{ fi.registerUrl }}">Files &rarr;</a>{% endif %}

    {% if not fi.measured %}
        {# NOTHING MEASURED IS NOT NOUGHT. No module on this installation
           keeps a file, so there is no number to draw and the cell says which
           of the two silences this is. #}
        <p class="zeb">No module keeps a file yet. A file arrives by being attached to a record, so the first one appears when a module that stores them is switched on in an area.</p>
    {% elseif fi.latest is empty %}
        <p class="zeb">Nothing has been kept in this period.</p>
    {% else %}
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr><th>file</th><th>module</th><th>area</th><th>kept</th><th>size</th></tr>
            {% for row in fi.latest %}
                <tr>
                    <td><b>{{ row.name }}</b></td>
                    <td>{{ row.moduleLabel|lower }}</td>
                    {# A FILE OUTSIDE EVERY AREA IS A FACT, not a blank: the
                       organization keeps files that belong to no area. #}
                    <td>{{ row.areaLabel ?? '—' }}</td>
                    <td><time datetime="{{ row.keptAt|date('c') }}" data-localtime-format="daystamp">{{ row.keptAt|date('j M H:i')|lower }}</time></td>
                    <td class="num">{{ row.byteSize|storage_bytes }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>
        <div class="sxfoot"><span>{{ fi.latest|length }} of {{ fi.total|number_format }} &middot; newest first &middot; kept on {{ fi.target }}</span></div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
